      "mutedcolors",
      "prisoncell",
      "tileset",
      "rpgmakermv"
    ],
    "description": "I thought I should maybe veer a bit back into making tilesets, and decided since I pretty much stopped working on these (I don't really like the color palette but am too lazy to change it) I might as well upload them! Some tiles are 24x24 based while others go straight for 48x48. There's a total of three parts to this: A2 (tiles that use a grid as basis), A5 (normal tiles) and B (objects etc); named as such since that's what the MV calls them.\n\nThis looks a bit more washed out and less colored compared to the rest. I wanted to make some 'standard' interior things like Bookshelves, chairs, benches because I can't draw convincing chairs, small desks, books, boxes, painting frames etc. and they all ended up as being brown. And then there's the cell parts, where I couldn't decide between solid black background or none and light blue versus gray. Oh, and some 'decorative' eyes for the walls that can open and close (top is closed eye, middle is transitioning, bottom is opened eye).\n\nThe painting frames have nothing in them because, well, I couldn't decide on what kinda painting to put in there,so I guess you gotta fill those frames all yourself.\n\nFree to use, whether it's the RPG Maker MV or not, and free to recolor as well since not even I am happy with the pallette. It'd be nice if you showed me where you used them, of course...",
